DTSTART:20261010T190000Z
DTEND:20261010T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261010T000000Z
SUMMARY:Silent Stage Series: An Immersive Headphone Experience
DESCRIPTION:THE SILENT STAGE SERIES\n\nAn Immersive Headphone Performance 
 Experience from the Jersey City Free Public Library\n\nFour locations. Four 
 performances. One unforgettable listening experience.\n\nExperience music 
 and movement in an entirely new way during The Silent Stage Series! Each 
 program invites guests to wear wireless headphones that deliver the live 
 performance\, music\, and instruction directly to their ears with 
 exceptional clarity. The result is an intimate and immersive experience 
 that preserves all the excitement and connection of enjoying a live 
 performance together.\n\nFrom ’90s hip-hop performed by a string quartet 
 and popular music reimagined on the piano to an expressive clarinet 
 performance and an interactive salsa class\, there is something for 
 everyone to experience!\n\nCapacity is limited to only 45 guests at each 
 performance. Advance registration is required separately for each 
 event.\n\n90’S HIP-HOP ON STRINGS WITH HIGHLINE STRING 
 QUARTET\n\nSaturday\, October 3\, 2026 | 3:30–4:30 p.m.\nKo Cafe\n722 
 Grand St\, Jersey City\, NJ 07304\n\nThe soundtrack of the ’90s meets the 
 power and elegance of live strings! Join the Highline String Quartet for an 
 unforgettable performance that reimagines the rhythm\, energy\, and 
 nostalgia of ’90s hip-hop through the rich sound of a professional string 
 ensemble.\n\nGuests will experience the quartet through wireless 
 headphones\, bringing every beat\, harmony\, and movement of the strings 
 directly to their ears. Whether you grew up with the music or are 
 discovering it for the first time\, this one-of-a-kind concert will have 
 you hearing a legendary era in a completely new way.\n\nHighline String 
 Quartet is a project of the Highline Chamber Ensemble\, a group of 
 passionate musicians known for presenting performances in nontraditional 
 concert spaces\, including lofts\, art galleries\, and studios. Highline 
 has regularly performed at celebrated New York City venues including 
 Joe’s Pub\, SubCulture\, and the Manderley Bar at Sleep No 
 More.\n\nInspired by New York City’s High Line Park\, the ensemble 
 represents the meeting of cultural preservation and contemporary society. 
 Its extensive network includes accomplished musicians with backgrounds from 
 institutions such as Harvard\, Princeton\, Yale\, Dartmouth\, Juilliard\, 
 and the Manhattan School of Music.\n\nCapacity is limited to 45 guests. 
 Reserve your headphones early!\n\nREGISTER HERE: 
 https://jerseycityfreepubliclibraryfoundation-bloom.kindful.com/e/90s-hip-hop-on-strings-silent-event-series\n\nCONTEMPORARY 
 CURRENTS WITH NELLYSMELODIES\n\nSaturday\, October 10\, 2026 | 3:00–4:00 
 p.m.\nVan Vorst Park\n257–287 Montgomery Street\, Jersey City\, NJ 
 07302\n\nExperience your favorite music reimagined at the piano during 
 Contemporary Currents with Nellysmelodies. From R&B and pop to hip-hop\, 
 gospel\, and contemporary favorites\, pianist Garnell Curtis transforms 
 familiar songs into expressive performances filled with emotion\, warmth\, 
 and creativity.\n\nGuests will listen to the live performance through 
 wireless headphones\, creating an up-close musical experience where every 
 note\, melody\, and subtle detail can be heard clearly—even in the middle 
 of the city.\n\nGarnell Curtis\, professionally known as Nellysmelodies\, 
 is a Connecticut-based pianist and content creator who transforms popular 
 songs into expressive piano performances. Classically trained and able to 
 play music by ear\, he blends R&B\, pop\, hip-hop\, gospel\, and 
 contemporary music to create engaging performances that connect with 
 audiences across generations. Above all\, his greatest goal is to put a 
 smile on someone’s face and make their day a little brighter through 
 music.\n\nCapacity is limited to 45 guests. Reserve your headphones 
 early!\n\nREGISTER HERE: 
 https://jerseycityfreepubliclibraryfoundation-bloom.kindful.com/e/contemporary-currents\n\nREEDS 
 IN RHYTHM WITH CANDYCE RAIFORD\n\nWednesday\, October 14\, 2026 | 6:00 
 p.m.\nGlenn D. Cunningham Branch Library Amphitheater\n275 Martin Luther 
 King Drive\, Jersey City\, NJ 07305\n\nGet ready for an intimate musical 
 experience where every note\, breath\, and rhythm comes alive. Reeds in 
 Rhythm invites audiences to discover the expressive sound and energy of 
 live music in a fresh\, immersive setting.\n\nCandyce Raiford is a 
 multi-instrumentalist originally from Indianapolis who fuses classical and 
 jazz with many genres—redefining what is possible for the clarinet. A 
 survivor of abortion\, foster care\, and a lifetime of neglect\, her life 
 exists because someone fought for her right to be born. As the 
 great-great-niece of Bass Reeves—the original Lone Ranger and first 
 African-American U.S. Marshal—and a Marine Corps veteran\, Candyce trains 
 in Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu\, creates self-produced work and cover tunes\, and 
 raises her children. Candyce believes everyone has purpose and can rise 
 from pain. Struggle is just the prelude to greatness.\n\nAudience members 
 will listen through wireless headphones\, bringing Candyce’s performance 
 directly to their ears with exceptional clarity. The result is a deeply 
 personal listening experience that still captures the energy and connection 
 of enjoying live music together.\n\nCapacity is limited to 45 guests. 
 Reserve your headphones and secure your spot today!\n\nREGISTER HERE: 
 https://jerseycityfreepubliclibraryfoundation-bloom.kindful.com/e/reeds-in-rhythm\n\nINTRO 
 TO SALSA DANCE WITH KENIA ROSETE DANCE\n\nSaturday\, October 17\, 2026 | 
 3:00 p.m.\nÀbáké Books & Cafe\n2 Webster Avenue\, Jersey City\, 
 NJ\n\nStep onto the dance floor and experience salsa in an entirely new 
 way! Led by Jersey City dancer\, choreographer\, and educator Kenia 
 Rosete\, this welcoming introductory class will guide participants through 
 the rhythm\, movement\, and joyful energy of salsa dance.\n\nParticipants 
 will wear wireless headphones that deliver the music and instruction 
 directly to them\, creating a clear\, personal connection to every beat 
 while sharing the excitement of dancing together. No previous dance 
 experience is necessary—just bring your enthusiasm and get ready to 
 move!\n\nKenia C. Rosete is a Mexican-American dancer\, choreographer\, 
 educator\, and producer based in Jersey City. Her work bridges social and 
 contemporary dance practices while exploring themes of migration\, 
 identity\, and relational movement. She is the founder of Kenia Rosete 
 Dance\, through which she creates original choreographic work\, curates the 
 FOCUS Innovative Choreography Series\, and leads community programs such as 
 The Art of Salsa Dance.\n\nCapacity is limited to 45 participants. Reserve 
 your headphones and spot on the dance floor early!\n\nREGISTER HERE: 
 https://jerseycityfreepubliclibraryfoundation-bloom.kindful.com/e/intro-to-salsa-the-silent-stage-series\n\nHELP 
 BRING MORE EXPERIENCES LIKE THIS TO JERSEY CITY\n\nPrograms like The Silent 
 Stage Series are made possible through community support. By donating to 
 the Jersey City Free Public Library Foundation\, you help the Library bring 
 more innovative\, accessible\, and unforgettable cultural experiences to 
 neighborhoods throughout Jersey City.\n\nEvery contribution—no matter the 
 amount—helps create opportunities for our community to learn\, connect\, 
 and experience something new. Please consider making a donation today and 
 help us keep exciting programs like these coming!\n\nFour locations. Four 
 performances. One unforgettable listening experience.\n
LOCATION:Offsite- please see description 
ORGANIZER;CN="Anthony Williams":MAILTO:awilliams@jclibrary.org
CATEGORIES:October, Popular Events > Music and Dance Events
